          "text": "Left corneal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pen torch examination shows a small central-paracentral whitish opacity, approximately 1–2 mm, consistent with the known ulcer; no gross corneal haze or obvious perforation."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
